{#
	Which logo a design prints (owner, 2026-11-09: the site logo "should appear on PDFs the site generates ... included in
	emails ... determined by admin on a per email template / design basis"): the site logo from Settings > Site Owner, a
	logo of the design's own, uploaded beside it, or none, as three feature cards, with the site logo shown so the choice
	is made by sight. Financial documents, certificate designs and email templates share it.
	lc: {name: the field (logo_choice when left out), value: a key of SiteLogo::CHOICES, site_logo: the site logo's
	address or null, what: what prints it, such as 'the documents', id: the cards' id, own_note: what the own card says,
	none_note: what the none card says, form: a form elsewhere on the page the cards belong to, or ''}.
#}
{% set lc_site_note = lc.site_logo ? 'The logo from Settings, Site Owner. Change it there and ' ~ lc.what ~ ' follow.' : 'None is uploaded yet: add it at Settings, Site Owner. Until then it is as if No logo were chosen.' %}
<div class="cl-logo-choice">
	{{ ui('form.picture-choice', {name: lc.name|default('logo_choice'), legend: 'Which logo', id: lc.id, size: 'small', selected: lc.value, form: lc.form|default(''), items: [
		{value: 'site', label: 'The site logo', icon: lucide('building-2'), note: lc_site_note},
		{value: 'own', label: 'A logo of its own', icon: lucide('image-plus'), note: lc.own_note},
		{value: 'none', label: 'No logo', icon: lucide('image-off'), note: lc.none_note},
	]}) }}
	{% if lc.site_logo %}<figure class="cl-logo-choice-site"><img src="{{ lc.site_logo }}" alt="The site logo"><figcaption>The site logo</figcaption></figure>{% endif %}
</div>
